Description: fprintd-compatible D-Bus service (net.reactivated.Fprint) for
 Synaptics/Validity match-on-chip fingerprint sensors
 validity-daemon serves fprintd's D-Bus API (net.reactivated.Fprint) for the
 Synaptics/Validity match-on-chip fingerprint sensors that libfprint does not
 support (06cb:009a: ThinkPad T480, T480s, X280, X1 Carbon 6th gen).
 pam_fprintd, fprintd's tools and desktops keep working unchanged. It replaces
 fprintd's daemon by taking over its D-Bus activation file only; removing this
 package gives fprintd its file back. PAM is not configured: enabling
 fingerprint login (always 'sufficient', never 'required') is the
 administrator's choice. The Synaptics vendor files, which may not be
 redistributed, are downloaded on installation by validity-vendor and checked by
 SHA-256.

